  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound [(2R,3R,4S,5R,6S)-2-(acetyloxymethyl)-6-[[(3S,4R,4aS)-4-ethenyl-8-oxo-4,4a,5,6-tetrahydro-3H-pyrano[3,4-c]pyran-3-yl]oxy]-3,5-dihydroxyoxan-4-yl] 2-hydroxy-3-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxybenzoate and HPAC, through the target of SNU-387. SNU-387 is a known target of multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and Licochalcone D, all of which are linked to HPAC. This suggests that the compound in question may share a common mechanism of action, potentially involving the activation or modulation of pathways that ultimately lead to HPAC being a target. The evidence points to a possible dependency on SNU-387, which is a key mediator in the interaction between the compound and HPAC, though the exact mechanism of this dependency remains to be fully elucidated.",
